      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For optimal stability, you should stick to column stacking heavy pallets, as it aligns with the racking system's design for stability and weight distribution. Interlocking is generally not recommended for high-density racking setups because of the potential for load shifting and increased tipping risks. Use load distribute straps or chains to secure the pallets to the racking during transit and ensure they are properly spaced. Investing in proper pallet supporting systems that are designed for the specific racking system can greatly improve safety and efficiency in your warehouse operations.",
